ession collapses once margin/state is matched; original finding was a score/context confound.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n_treated team=15614, star=2481\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF30"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-075", "score": 0.102, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-075 | Study family SF-APPS-075: Extended Possession Value (direct PPP + opponent T+1 suppression)\n- observed_research_question: Extended Possession Value (direct PPP + opponent T+1 suppression)\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: Play types and players have a real downstream (opponent next-PPP) component beyond direct PPP.\n- observed_result: 4/8 PTs downstream real: CUT Ext 1.658 (supp +0.0220), TRANSITION 1.509 (+0.0145), SPOT_UP 1.303 (+0.0124), POST_UP 1.127 (+0.0194). DRIVE downstream not real (opp ATT +0.0024). Player downstream mostly BH ns except M. M [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Downstream effects are small (~0.01-0.02 PPP) relative to direct PPP gaps; player list is mostly non-FINDING after BH.\n- observed_sample_and_power: PT-level n in the tens to hundreds of thousands implied by other seq files\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-049\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF07"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-086", "score": 0.101, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-086 | Study family SF-CHT-086: LLM / ex-ante usefulness of suppression context (leakage audit)\n- observed_research_question: LLM / ex-ante usefulness of suppression context (leakage audit)\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: An LLM layer can reason about suppression context beyond the engine, or predicting suppression from H1 is a viable label.\n- observed_result: Label is mostly an RTM artifact. Apparent LLM skill was leakage; what survives is small/noisy; engine misses are selection/override not missing graph facts. Margin of 